  "result": "The VAT feature is now complete with all 91 tests passing. Here's a summary of the implementation:\n\n## VAT (Value Added Tax) Feature\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n   - Imported `roundCents` from money module for proper VAT rounding\n   - Added `lineVat()` function to calculate VAT per line on amount after discount\n   - Each line's VAT is rounded individually using banker's rounding\n   - Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - Formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n\n2. **Updated `src/render.js`:**\n   - Modified to show VAT line before total (only if VAT > 0)\n   - Displays `VAT: \u20acX.XX` above the total line\n\n3. **Updated tests in `test/invoices.test.js`:**\n   - Updated 6 existing invoiceTotals tests to account for VAT\n   - Added 7 new tests covering:\n     - 0% VAT rates\n     - Mixed VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n     - VAT calculation on discounted amounts\n     - Per-line VAT rounding\n     - Combined discount and VAT scenarios\n\n4. **Updated tests in `test/render.test.js`:**\n   - Fixed line count assertions (now includes VAT line)\n   - Updated total expectations to include VAT\n\n**Key VAT behavior:**\n- VAT is calculated per line on the amount AFTER discount is applied\n- Each line's VAT is rounded individually (banker's rounding)\n- Invoice's VAT is the sum of all rounded line VATs\n- VAT line only appears if there's VAT to display\n\nReady to commit when approved.",
